alue "125485"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "126229"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "127112"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "127929"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "128645"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "129448"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "130607"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "131707"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "132777"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "133505"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "134093"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "263735"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "332138"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "355588"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "2007854"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/660"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Middleweight, Greco-Roman (≤77 kg), Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "2 –  3 August 2021"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2125"} "Makuhari Messe, 2-1, Nakase, Mihama-ku, Chiba, Chiba Prefecture, Japan"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/19009358"} "15 from 15 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/117165"} "Tamás Lőrincz"] " was competing in his fourth Olympics for Hungary. He had won silver in 2012 at 66 kg, but was a four-time World Championship medallist, highlighted by his 2019 title in this class after silvers in 2015 and 2017. He came to Tokyo seeded first. The second seed went to Sweden’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/146779"} "Alex Kessidis"] ", but he would lose his opening match to Azerbaijani " [:a {:href "/athletes/140928"} "Rafiq Hüseynov"] " on a judges’ decision after they tied, 1-1."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Lőrincz would add Olympic gold to his " [:em {} "palmarès"] " but was far from dominant. He won in round one by a forfeit and then won his final three bouts by decision, all by margins of 1 or 2 points. In the final Lőrincz  faced Kyrgyzstan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/144879"} "Akzhol Makhmudov"] ", defeating him 2-1 in a dull match. One day later, Tamás Lőrincz’s brother " [:a {:href "/athletes/134403"} "Viktor"] " would add a silver medal to the family trophy chest by placing second at 87 kg Greco-Roman. Makhmudov was a 2018 Asian Champion but had only made it to the Olympics by winning an Olympic qualifying tournament earlier in 2021."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The repêchage rounds went completely against the betting favorites, as both losing semi-finalists lost to finish equal fifth. Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/144747"} "Shohei Yabiku"] " had a bye to the repêchage final where he defeated Iranian " [:a {:href "/athletes/143833"} "Mohammadali Geraei"] ", who had lost his semi to Lőrincz. Azerbaijan’s Hüseynov won his opening match in the repêchage and then took bronze by defeating Armenian " [:a {:href "/athletes/140552"} "Karapet Chalyan"] ", who had been defeated by Makhmudov in their semi-final."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Classification Points", :class "footnote"} "CP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Fall", :class "footnote"} "VF"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Technical Superiority", :class "footnote"} "ST"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points", :class "footnote"} "TP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points Received", :class "footnote"} "TPR"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/117165"} "Tamás Lőrincz"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middl